CATEGORIZATION RULES (IMPORTANT, in order):

1. Prefer abstention over a wrong guess. Respond with {"type": "skip"} when no existing category clearly fits. Skipped transactions stay uncategorized for manual review.

2. Use the per-category description, examples ("Beispiele:") and disambiguation ("Hinweis:") above as your primary guide. A weak or speculative association is NOT enough — skip instead.

3. Self-transfers (a payee that is the user's own name with an IBAN in parentheses) are typically savings transfers — see the description of the "Savings" category. Classify them; do NOT skip them just because the payee is a personal name.

4. Do not suggest new categories unless the transaction clearly belongs to a domain that no existing category covers.

RESPONSE FORMAT: respond with ONLY a valid JSON object in one of these shapes:

{"type": "existing", "categoryId": "<uuid>"}
{"type": "rule", "categoryId": "<uuid>", "ruleName": "string"}
{"type": "new", "newCategory": {"name": "string", "groupName": "string", "groupIsNew": boolean}}
{"type": "skip"}

DO NOT output any text before or after the JSON. Your entire response must be a valid, parsable JSON object.

